(6104024, 897883, 30982, '<td valign="top">Now this is the way to play the challenge - really beat the carp out of your own first score and get a new personal best and a top ten at the same time!  Well done!</td>', 'Now this is the way to play the challenge - really beat the carp out of your own first score and get a new personal best and a top ten at the same time!  Well done!', '2010-07-26 01:15:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6104025, 898145, 66515, '<td valign="top">So um..does this mean you are on the frontpage twice for the same challenge since the 2nd place image was a recreation of one of yours? :)<br/> <br/>Thank you for sharing this fantastic image and congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'So um..does this mean you are on the frontpage twice for the same challenge since the 2nd place image was a recreation of one of yours? :) Thank you for sharing this fantastic image and congrats on the ribbon.', '2010-07-26 01:15:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6104026, 898137, 68947, '<td valign="top">Nice job Carrie! :)  I know that technically, there is a bit of a blow-out on the right side wing BUT... the idea of this original challenge was "Light On White" and the harsher lighting FITS with the idea behind this shot..."Child of The Light" LOL :)  It works well, Carrie.  I think there are going to be people who will look mostly at the technicals and not the entire shot as a whole and others who will do all.  To be honest...the subject was not a great one when I did it back in 2006! LOL  I''m very honored and congrats.  You did an excellent job on what DPCers frown upon usually....a shot of a statue LOL ;)</td>', 'Nice job Carrie! :)  I know that technically, there is a bit of a blow-out on the right side wing BUT... the idea of this original challenge was "Light On White" and the harsher lighting FITS with the idea behind this shot..."Child of The Light" LOL :)  It works well, Carrie.  I think there are going to be people who will look mostly at the technicals and not the entire shot as a whole and others who will do all.  To be honest...the subject was not a great one when I did it back in 2006! LOL  I''m very honored and congrats.  You did an excellent job on what DPCers frown upon usually....a shot of a statue LOL ;)', '2010-07-26 01:15:28.000000', NULL, 0);
